-- title:
--   Theorem 1, p. 9 — □ VaR^{Λᵢ}_{αᵢ} = VaR^Λ_{Σαᵢ}, with an optimal allocation of the form (9)
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,\mathbb P)$ be an atomless probability space, $n\ge1$, $\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_n>0$ with $\alpha=\sum_{i=1}^n\alpha_i<1$, and $\Lambda_1,\dots,\Lambda_n\in\{L,R\}$. Put $\Lambda=L$ if $\Lambda_1=\dots=\Lambda_n=L$ and $\Lambda=R$ otherwise. Let $X$ be a random variable.
--
--   1. The inf-convolution of the VaRs is a VaR at the summed level:
--   $$\mathop{\square}_{i=1}^n\mathrm{VaR}^{\Lambda_i}_{\alpha_i}(X)=\mathrm{VaR}^\Lambda_\alpha(X).$$
--   2. There is a partition $(A_1,\dots,A_n)$ of $\Omega$ such that
--   $$X_i=(X-\mathrm{VaR}^\Lambda_\alpha(X))\mathbb 1_{A_i}+\frac1n\mathrm{VaR}^\Lambda_\alpha(X),\qquad i=1,\dots,n,\qquad(9)$$
--   is an optimal allocation of $X$ for $(\mathrm{VaR}^{\Lambda_1}_{\alpha_1},\dots,\mathrm{VaR}^{\Lambda_n}_{\alpha_n})$.
--   3. For every partition $(A_1,\dots,A_n)$ of $\Omega$ that is independent of $X$ and has $\mathbb P(A_i)=\alpha_i/\alpha$ for $i=1,\dots,n$, the allocation (9) is optimal.
--
--   The theorem gives the full picture for agents who all use quantile-based capital requirements: the minimal total capital for a risk $X$ is a quantile of $X$ at the summed level, it is a right quantile as soon as one agent uses a right quantile, and it is attained by giving every agent an equal share of the capital and the excess loss to one agent selected by the partition.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The domain is $L^0$ (measurable random variables) and the inf-convolution is computed in $[-\infty,\infty]$; part 1 asserts it equals a real number. Part 1 is stated for the given $X$, which is arbitrary. A partition consists of measurable, pairwise disjoint sets covering $\Omega$, possibly some empty. Independence in part 3 is Mathlib's independence of the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $A_1,\dots,A_n$ and the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $X$. Atomlessness is the paper's standing assumption (§2.1) and is kept for all three parts.
-- source:
--   Liu, Mao, Wang & Wei, Inf-convolution, Optimal Allocations, and Model Uncertainty for Tail Risk Measures, SSRN 3490348 (version of January 16, 2022), p. 9, Theorem 1 and display (9); proof pp. 9–12

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TailRiskSharing_VaRConv_Setting

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace TailRiskSharing.VaRConv

theorem theorem1_var_inf_convolution {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω]
    (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P] (hP : IsAtomless P)
    (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (αs : Fin n → ℝ) (hα : ∀ i, 0 < αs i) (hsum : ∑ i, αs i < 1)
    (Λs : Fin n → Side) (X : Ω → ℝ) (hX : X ∈ (L0 : Set (Ω → ℝ))) :
    -- (i)
    infConv L0 (fun i => VaRS P (Λs i) (αs i)) X =
      ((VaRS P (aggSide Λs) (∑ i, αs i) X : ℝ) : EReal) ∧
    -- (ii)
    (∃ A : Fin n → Set Ω, IsMeasPartition A ∧
      IsOptimalAllocation L0 (fun i => VaRS P (Λs i) (αs i)) X
        (partitionAllocation X (VaRS P (aggSide Λs) (∑ i, αs i) X) A)) ∧
    -- (iii)
    (∀ A : Fin n → Set Ω, IsMeasPartition A →
      (∀ i, P (A i) = ENNReal.ofReal (αs i / ∑ j, αs j)) →
      Indep (MeasurableSpace.generateFrom (Set.range A))
        (MeasurableSpace.comap X inferInstance) P →
      IsOptimalAllocation L0 (fun i => VaRS P (Λs i) (αs i)) X
        (partitionAllocation X (VaRS P (aggSide Λs) (∑ i, αs i) X) A)) := by sorry

end TailRiskSharing.VaRConv
